# Data (not stored in this repo)

The data files are too large for GitHub. Download them from Zenodo and place them
in the same folder as the scripts.

## ALPHA-g simulation (Zenodo record 13963779)
Link: https://zenodo.org/records/13963779

| Role | Filename | SHA-256 |
|---|---|---|
| Validation (chooses D0_MAX) | spacepoint_vertices_simulation_0-310_val_light-wireamp0-runnum0-sim1.h5 | 3FE371CDB7F8B3997FE7AB1B0C698E3E5D0FF5D918B89F762714E4119734857B |
| Test (final results) | [exact filename].h5 | [64-character hash] |

## MicroBooNE overlay sample (Zenodo record 7261921)
Link: https://zenodo.org/records/7261921

| Role | Filename | SHA-256 |
|---|---|---|
| Development | nue_NoWire_19.h5 | C1BC4A45ECBA3F16CC4FD8EB40C57B1A53BC803F238570DDBD1D539F2A069F32C191CB0C09E94BE0810C25F498DEEC56898FBD97417FFA48D2116A413C770B4B |
| Test | [exact filename] | [64-character hash] |

To verify your download:
- Windows: `Get-FileHash [filename] -Algorithm SHA256`
- Mac/Linux: `sha256sum [filename]`

The output must match the table above.

## Reproducing the results
    python run.py run [validation file] [test file] --n 3000
    python ablate.py [validation file] [test file] --n 3000
    python stress.py
    python ub_run.py [development file] [test file] --n 100
